{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#organization",
      "name": "THE ONREPEAT",
      "legalName": "SUNYE ATTIRE PRIVATE LIMITED",
      "alternateName": ["THE ONREPEAT CLOTHING", "ONREPEAT", "OnRepeat", "Shunya", "SUन्य", "शून्य", "theonrepeat"],
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "{{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 400 | prepend: 'https:' }}",
        "width": 400
      },
      "description": "Premium apparel brand from India, inspired by Sanskrit philosophy and fifth-century Indian art. Founded in 2024 by Paras Soni.",
      "slogan": "From Zero to Infinite",
      "foundingDate": "2024-08-07",
      {%- comment -%}
        Government-registry identifiers. These are the only facts about this brand that a third party
        can independently verify today — MCA for the CIN, the GST portal for the GSTIN — so they carry
        real weight on "is this a real business" queries where no earned coverage exists yet.
        PAN and TAN are deliberately not published. (The GSTIN embeds the PAN by construction, which
        is normal and unavoidable in India.)
      {%- endcomment -%}
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "CIN",
          "name": "Corporate Identity Number (India)",
          "value": "U46419HR2024PTC124013"
        },
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "GSTIN",
          "name": "Goods and Services Tax Identification Number (India)",
          "value": "09ABOCS0725J1ZZ"
        }
      ],
      "taxID": "09ABOCS0725J1ZZ",
      "founder": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Paras Soni",
        "jobTitle": "Founder"
      },
      "sameAs": [
        "{{ settings.social_instagram_link }}",
        "{{ settings.social_facebook_link }}",
        "{{ settings.social_youtube_link }}",
        "https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-onrepeat",
        "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/the-onrepeat"
      ],
      "areaServed": {
        "@type": "Country",
        "name": "India",
        "@id": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q668"
      },
      "countryOfOrigin": {
        "@type": "Country",
        "name": "India"
      },
      "hasOfferCatalog": {
        "@type": "OfferCatalog",
        "name": "THE ONREPEAT Apparel Collection",
        "url": "{{ shop.url }}/collections"
      },
      "contactPoint": {
        "@type": "ContactPoint",
        "contactType": "customer service",
        "email": "support@theonrepeat.co",
        "availableLanguage": ["English", "Hindi"],
        "areaServed": "IN"
      },
      {%- comment -%}
        Two addresses, because they are two different legal things and the site was previously
        publishing them unlabelled — the Terms carried the registered office, the Privacy Policy
        carried the operating address, and a reader (or a parser) saw a contradiction.
        `address` is the registered office on the Certificate of Incorporation; `location` is the
        principal place of business on the GST registration.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "name": "Registered office",
        "streetAddress": "C/O Rajesh Kumar, W. No. 10, Nr. State Bank, Ellenabad",
        "addressLocality": "Sirsa",
        "addressRegion": "Haryana",
        "postalCode": "125102",
        "addressCountry": "IN"
      },
      "location": {
        "@type": "Place",
        "name": "Principal place of business",
        "address": {
          "@type": "PostalAddress",
          "streetAddress": "Ground Floor, 005, Tower B, Sector 132",
          "addressLocality": "Noida",
          "addressRegion": "Uttar Pradesh",
          "postalCode": "201304",
          "addressCountry": "IN"
        }
      },
      "knowsLanguage": ["en", "hi", "sa"],
      "knowsAbout": ["Premium Apparel", "Sanskrit Heritage", "Indian Fashion", "Apparel Design", "Youth Fashion India", "Sustainable Fashion India", "Indian Apparel Brand", "Sanskrit Philosophy"]
      {%- comment -%}
        subjectOf removed. It asserted three separate Article nodes — "featured in The Tribune",
        "…The Print", "…WBN" — none of which carried a url, so none could be checked. They were also
        not three features: all three are the same VMPL press release distributed through ANI on
        19 Aug 2025, and the outlets label it as such (ThePrint files it under /ani-press-releases/
        and prints an advertorial disclaimer). Three unverifiable Article claims for one syndicated
        release reads as inflation to anything that checks. Press is presented, accurately labelled,
        on the About page instead — where a reader can see what it is.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#website",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      "name": "THE ONREPEAT",
      "publisher": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#organization" },
      "potentialAction": {
        "@type": "SearchAction",
        "target": {
          "@type": "EntryPoint",
          "urlTemplate": "{{ shop.url }}/search?q={search_term_string}"
        },
        "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#webpage",
      "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
      {%- comment -%}
        Read from page_title rather than repeated by hand, so this node, the <title> tag and the
        homepage <h1> in snippets/header-logo.liquid all state the same page name. They used to
        differ by the "| OnRepeat · Shunya" tail, which is one more conflicting name for a search
        engine choosing what to print above a result.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      "name": {{ page_title | default: 'THE ONREPEAT — Premium apparel from India' | json }},
      "isPartOf": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#website" },
      "about": { "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#organization" },
      "description": "From Zero to Infinite. Premium apparel inspired by Sanskrit philosophy. Hoodies, t-shirts, shirts and sweatshirts. Free shipping in India.",
      "speakable": {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        "cssSelector": [".heading", ".rte"]
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
